# The over-cap tome fix (inc-bsqm), played for real: an orc barbarian fills
# his Constitution inherent bonus to the cap with one tome, goes ABOVE the
# cap by the one live route the game offers, then reads a second tome.
# Read by tools/check_inh_wasteful_play.sh.
#
# The over-cap route: only the shambling mound's electricity handler
# (lib/mon3.irh:2100-2103) grants an uncapped +1d4 ADJUST_INH A_CON, and only
# a player in mound form can reach it. Wizard mode supplies what a player
# cannot roll for in a short script -- the tomes, the transformation, a
# weak monster to provide the electric hit -- but the tome read that is
# actually under test happens through the ordinary 'r' command, and the
# result is read off the screen, not an internal probe.
#
#   w y                            wizard mode
#   Item Acquisition -> Tomes      walk to "]: Tomes" (RIGHT from the first
#                                   category), then to "Libram of Bodily
#                                   Health" (the Constitution tome)
#   ENTER "5" ENTER                take it at +5: one read grants e.vDmg=5,
#                                   which exactly fills the cap for a
#                                   character with no CA_INHERANT_POTENTIAL
#                                   (MaxBonus = 5 + AbilityLevel(...) = 5)
#   @while "Air'" s                 the item lands 'In the Air'; this label
#                                   stays on screen even once the slot is
#                                   empty, so the loop always "gives up"
#                                   after stowing on the first press -- a
#                                   known, harmless idiom, not a failure
#   r -> (in pack) Libram...        read it: CON's inherent bonus is now at
#                                   the cap (5)
#   [repeat acquisition]           a second +5 Libram, left in the pack for
#                                   the real test below
#   Polymorph the PC ->
#     Plant Creatures ->
#     Shambling mound               Shapeshift(), the same call Wild Shape
#                                   and a polymorph item use. The "falls
#                                   free" message that follows uses
#                                   "-- more --", not "--More--" -- a
#                                   different prompt style from the tome
#                                   read's, so the two dismiss loops use
#                                   different literal text
#   Monster Summoning -> TAB ->
#     Vermin -> grid bug            a CR -4 vermin whose only attack is
#                                   "A_BITE for 1d3 AD_ELEC" (lib/mon4.irh)
#                                   -- weak enough that the mound's 165 HP
#                                   and electricity immunity are never in
#                                   question, but its bite is lightning
#                                   damage, and ANY electricity hit on a
#                                   mound-formed creature runs the handler
#                                   that grants the uncapped +1d4, win or
#                                   lose on the enclosing attack roll
#   s*30                            wait while the bug attacks; the seed is
#                                   fixed, so the same hit lands the same
#                                   way every run (confirmed: "Grid Bug's
#                                   Attack ... [hit] ... 1 Lightning" at the
#                                   first wait on seed 1)
#   r -> (in pack) Libram...        read the second tome. This is the call
#                                   under test: the character is now ABOVE
#                                   the cap, not merely at it, because the
#                                   bug's temporary ADJUST_INH stacks with
#                                   the tome's permanent one.
#
# A wand needed a Use Magic Device check most barbarians fail outright (DC
# 18 vs a +1 or so modifier); the grid bug's melee attack needs no check
# from the player at all, so it is the more reliable route in a short,
# deterministic script.
#
# 'a' (KY_CMD_ACTIVATE) lists only worn wondrous items, not wands -- wands
# use 'b' (KY_CMD_BLAST_WAND, src/Player.cpp:559-560). @choose needs the
# "(in pack) " prefix FindMenuEntry actually draws (src/Wposix.cpp
# MenuLabel/NameMatches match from the start of the line, not a substring
# search), which is also why this script always writes out "(in pack)
# Libram of Bodily Health", never just the item name.
@include chargen.keys
w
y

# tome 1: fill CON to the cap
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Tomes" RIGHT
@until "Libram of Bodily Health" DOWN
@expect "Libram of Bodily Health"
DOWN
ENTER
"5" ENTER
@while "Air'" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
r
@choose "(in pack) Libram of Bodily Health"
@while "--More--" ENTER
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

# tome 2: acquire, leave in the pack for the over-cap read below
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Tomes" RIGHT
@until "Libram of Bodily Health" DOWN
@expect "Libram of Bodily Health"
DOWN
ENTER
"5" ENTER
@while "Air'" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

# polymorph into a shambling mound
w
@choose "Polymorph the PC"
@until "]: Plant Creatures" RIGHT
@until "Shambling mound" DOWN
@expect "Shambling mound"
DOWN
ENTER
@while "-- more --" ENTER

d
@dump:sheet-at-cap
@until "HP:" ESC

# summon a grid bug (1d3 AD_ELEC bite) next to the mound
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Vermin"
@choose "grid bug"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:summoned

s*30
@dump:elec-hit

d
@dump:sheet-over-cap
@until "HP:" ESC

# read tome 2 -- above the cap, the call under test
r
@dump:read-menu-2
@choose "(in pack) Libram of Bodily Health"
@while "--More--" ENTER
@dump:read-result

d
@dump:sheet-post-read
@until "HP:" ESC
@quit
